\scene[name=places-a, palette=night]{
  \frame[cols=4-9, cols@tablet=2-7, cols@phone=all, measure=620px]{
    \lede{Ask people where they do their best thinking and they rarely name a room built for it. They name a corner. A bench. The table nearest the window. These are some of those corners.}

    A good place to think seems to share a few things, whatever it looks like. It is a little untidy, so nothing is too precious to touch. It has light that changes through the day. And it holds evidence of earlier work, so that you never quite start from nothing.
  }
  \group[layout=row, cols=all, valign=stretch, gap=24px]{
